## Your calls

1. **English accent.** The grader called the "all Guy Ritchie's fault" parenthetical an insert, so I cut it. It was the page's only answer to the live query "why does madonna have an english accent." If you want that query, a sixth FAQ is a better home than the body.
2. **Length.** Reaching the 3,900 band means overriding the jury on protected passages; the next candidates are the Leonard block and the family-deaths paragraph. I left them alone.

Lint still warns that `published: true` disagrees with `production_pretext.status: draft`; I didn't touch that field, or `lastmod`, `date` or `content_quality`.

## What happens next

The pipeline clears the consumed review sidecar and re-grades. Targeted perspective verification must rerun, since the reader-visible text changed. `revision-resolution.md` is in the review directory, listing every changed line with its source; the short version is the `REVISION PASS NOTES` block at the bottom of the draft.
